{"id":"odu-mcp-rerun-doc","parent":"oduc-agent","ord":"a0","title":"odu: the MCP hides its single-lane retry","todo":true,"desc":"When one lane of a multi-platform run fails, the right move is to re-run that one lane — it works on a LIVE run, alongside the still-running sibling, cancelling nothing. The tool that does it, `node_rerun`, ships with NO description at all: an agent sees a bare `id` parameter and no hint of what it is for.\n\nMeanwhile `run`'s own description says \"one run per checkout\" and offers `supersede` prominently — which restarts the whole run and kills the other lanes. So the cheap correct operation is invisible and the expensive destructive one is the documented one. An agent reasoning from the tool surface concludes it must throw away a running darwin lane to retry a flaky linux one; that happened, and a person had to correct it.\n\nWanted: a real description on `node_rerun` (what it does, that it works mid-run, that nothing else is cancelled), a cross-reference from `run`/`supersede` saying this is the way to retry one lane, and the same correction wherever agents read odu's docs.\n\n**NOT A LANE — IT SHIPS INSIDE `odu-wait-settle-short`'s PR (the human, 2026-08-31 ~20:45).** So it carries no step subtree and takes no day-board row: a day-board row asserts a lane, and a lane with no steps is the flat-lane defect the dag names. The carrying lane's `see` edge is the binding; this item's mark moves when that PR merges.","created":"2026-08-31T16:53:16-04:00","changed":"2026-08-31T21:08:22-04:00","custom":{"from":"juspay/odu#34 (srid, 2026-06-19), moved here 2026-08-31 when odu's issues came to the vault"}}
{"id":"odu-green-exit-nonzero","parent":"oduc-runs","ord":"a0","title":"odu: a green run can still exit non-zero","done":"2026-08-31T18:01:57-04:00","started":"2026-08-31T16:55:33-04:00","worked":3984,"desc":"Reported 2026-06-11 as juspay/odu#18, moved to this vault 2026-08-31 and dispatched to grok the same day.\n\nThe claim: every node passes, the green statuses post — and the process still exits non-zero, because something failed while tearing down the remote ssh connection after the verdict was already in.\n\nGROUNDED (grok, 2026-08-31): the bug is dead, and the exit code never could see teardown — it is computed from node statuses at src/cli/render.ts:139. What produced the false failures was an unhandled stream error on the way out (EPIPE, later sealed-log throws) killing the coordinator, closed across odu #25, #33 and #93. Proved by killing the runner after an all-green run and getting 0. PR #95 therefore PINS the behaviour rather than fixing it: a unit test, the green e2e refusing the old crash signatures, and a kill-after-green case. Two review rounds sharpened it — the first pin was vacuous (it survived dropping the very clause it named), and the kill test could pass as a degraded run where no recipe node ever went green; both closed structurally.\n\n**odu's CI is BOTH (learned here, 2026-08-31): GitHub Actions AND odu's own dogfood.** The ruleset requires fourteen `ci::<recipe>@<platform>` contexts across both platforms, and those are posted by an actual odu run — the GHA jobs are not required checks. A watcher that only follows the Actions jobs leaves the PR BLOCKED with everything visibly green.","created":"2026-08-31T16:53:16-04:00","changed":"2026-08-31T18:01:57-04:00","custom":{"agent":"agent-grok","brief":"briefs/odu-green-exit.md","dispatched":"2026-08-31T17:00:00-04:00","from":"juspay/odu#18 (srid, 2026-06-11), moved here 2026-08-31","kolu-terminal":"958365fa","merge":"merge-auto","merge-commit":"https://github.com/juspay/odu/commit/374c16c2","merged":"2026-08-31","odu-worktree":".worktrees/green-exit","pr-url":"https://github.com/juspay/odu/pull/95","repo":"repo-odu","tier":"ordinary","timings":"investigate+PR 14m (grok) · review 5m (opus, 1 MUST) · address 12m · review 10m (pi, 1 new SHOULD) · address 4m · re-verdict 4m · ci 18/18 both platforms · close <1m — TOTAL ~1h06m (16:55→18:01)"}}
{"id":"odu-recipe-groups","parent":"oduc-recipes","ord":"a0","title":"odu: name a group of recipes and run it","todo":true,"desc":"To run part of a pipeline today you must spell out every recipe by name — there is no way to say \"the build group\" or \"the fast checks\". Wanted: define a named group once, then select it with one word, from the command line and through the agent interface alike.\n\nWhy it matters more for agents than for people: a person can keep a list in their head, but an agent has to know and repeat every recipe name to scope a run, and gets it wrong or gives up and runs everything.","created":"2026-08-31T16:53:16-04:00","changed":"2026-08-31T16:54:07-04:00","custom":{"from":"juspay/odu#16 (srid, 2026-06-11), moved here 2026-08-31"}}
{"id":"odu-bun-attach","parent":"oduc-runtime","ord":"a0","title":"odu: should the attach face move to bun? #needs-brainstorm","todo":true,"desc":"A decision record, not a task: should odu leave node+tsx for bun, mainly to unlock OpenTUI for the attach face?\n\nWhat the June research established. odu is on node by packaging convenience, not by a considered choice. OpenTUI's native renderer needs bun's FFI — under node it throws — though it has since started running on current-line node behind an experimental flag, which nixpkgs' LTS node does not have. So bun is the viable path today and node may be the path in six to twelve months. The real risk of a full port is that bun's weakest area (child processes, stdio teardown) is exactly odu's core competency, and unit tests on node would not catch it. The pull beyond widgets is that kolu's reactive hooks are Solid-only, so an OpenTUI+Solid terminal could share view code with a browser observer.\n\nThe recommendation on file, still the sensible one: do not port the runner. Prototype the ATTACH FACE on bun — read-only, no process supervision, smallest blast radius — and decide the rest afterwards. Cheapest first step either way: re-probe OpenTUI's renderer under current node with the experimental FFI flag and see how real that path has become.","created":"2026-08-31T16:53:16-04:00","changed":"2026-08-31T16:54:07-04:00","custom":{"from":"juspay/odu#27 (srid, 2026-06-12), moved here 2026-08-31 — the research and its recommendation preserved"}}
