{"id":"lane-oge-review","parent":"odu-green-exit-nonzero","ord":"a3","title":"review: pi","done":"2026-08-31T17:50:51-04:00","started":"2026-08-31T17:47:27-04:00","worked":1641,"after":["lane-oge-fix"],"created":"2026-08-31T17:10:46-04:00","changed":"2026-08-31T17:50:51-04:00","custom":{"kolu-terminal":"63cb4db3","musts":"0","reviewer":"agent-pi","shoulds":"1","verdict":"All three prior findings verified fixed at 97c61a8a — the unit pin fails under both on-paper mutations (cancelled clause, done gate), the false name is gone and odu.test.ts:576 exercises a teardown-shaped overlay, and the reworded comment states the true invariant. The e2e's death-observed proof checked EMPIRICALLY (one probe): an attached kill writes the lane-died line and exits 0, a kill that loses to idle-reap exits 0 without it — the assertion is load-bearing. NEW SHOULD the first pass missed: the wait predicate every(seen === \"success\") at transport-death.e2e.test.ts:276-284 is satisfied by _ci-setup alone while alpha/beta are still pending, so a kill there skips them into a state summarize calls clean — a degraded pass where no recipe node went green. Fix: enumerate the known set like the sibling test. NITs: grep stderr on close rather than exit; the mirrored-overlay drift chain. Comment 5485021230.","verdict-followup":"re-verdict at ef799c5a: SHIP IT — the degraded-pass leg is structurally gone (Map.get on an unseen recipe is undefined, so the _ci-setup-alone window cannot exist; the idle backstop moved 3s→30s for stall budget); the close-before-grep holds (whenClosed registered at spawn, awaited after exit) and hardens the stdout grep too; the overlay extraction audited arm-by-arm against the old branch as behaviour-preserving, with the unit test now pinning the real function across all seven statuses, so an ok-reterminalizing edit fails locally without the e2e. No probe needed."}}
